<title>HONG KONG: Simsen Metals interim net down 23.67 pct.</title>
<headline>Simsen Metals interim net down 23.67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended October 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   1.89	vs 2.96</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    nil	 vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  4.22 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    4.74	vs 6.22</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,325.76  vs 1,474.95</p>
<p>    Company name		 Simsen Metals (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Simsen trades nonferrous metals and ores, mainly copper, aluminium and nickel.</p>
<p>The company changed its financial year-end to April 30 from December 31. Comparative figures are for six-months ended June 30, 1995.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of a subsidiary company, the main asset of which is an indirect interest in a property development in Shanghai.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
